<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31421" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nŭmīcĭus</span></b> , a,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the name of a
				Roman</i> gens. So, L. Numicius Circeiensis, <i><span class="en">Liv. 8,
			3</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">T. Numicius Priscus,</span>”
				<i>a consul</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. 2,
					63</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ti. Numicius,</span>”
				<i>a tribune of the people</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Off. 3, 30, 109</span></i>
			: Minucius Thermus. <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 16, 20</span></i>. To Numicius is
			addressed <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 6</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
